{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_session_84_combined_handoff", "label": "Session 84 Combined Handoff", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-84-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_session_84_combined_stat84b", "label": "pack84/stat84b.py (Live-Lever Stationary Driver)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-84-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Repair by conf82's pattern on the class the chain actually uses: _Seeded(hfc2.HFC) whose seed() falls through when P0 is None, so a first pass reproduces sealed values bit-for-bit. LEVER_LIVE and DOUBT_EXERCISED are cleared BY RECEIPT, not by a hand-editable flag."}, {"id": "recovered_session_84_combined_semi84", "label": "semi84.py (Semiclassical Defect Instrument)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-84-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_session_84_combined_anchor_theorem", "label": "The Anchor Theorem (I = pi/L Exactly, for Any Charge and Any Bound E)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-84-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In u=1/r the radicand is a quadratic for constant q, so a bare nucleus of charge 90 and a hydrogen atom contribute identically. The whole l-dependence of the defect therefore lives in the region where q(r) VARIES - the first derived property of F_core in the project."}, {"id": "recovered_session_84_combined_dg_dl_criterion", "label": "dg/dl = 2 - J, so G-within <=> J < 2", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-84-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_session_84_combined_lever_live_receipt", "label": "Lever Live by Receipt (pack84/lever84.json)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-84-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_session_84_combined_s5_inversion", "label": "The Centrifugal Barrier Parks a Channel in the Transition Region", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-84-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Filed expectation was that penetrating channels deviate most from the anchor; measured 0.599 for l<=1 against 0.835 for l>=3, the other way round. The barrier does not protect a high-l channel from the core, it parks it in the only region the anchor does not cancel."}, {"id": "recovered_session_84_combined_orbital_collapse_two_wells", "label": "Z=89 5f: Two Allowed Regions Split by a Centrifugal Barrier", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-84-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The orbital-collapse configuration appearing unbidden at actinium - the only channel of thirty returning an inner and an outer well."}, {"id": "recovered_session_84_combined_f84_3", "label": "F84.3 Exchange Localisation Diverges at Every Node of P", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-84-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The X/P localisation split a 4s radicand into four false regions, which F84.2's region-finder would have read as the collapse physics it exists to detect. Ruled to the direct core field, where 1 <= q <= Z by Gauss's law."}, {"id": "recovered_session_84_combined_f84_1", "label": "F84.1 f811 Blind to a Restart Written as step